Z||000000||Jaygee79||08-22-2001||12:37 AM||||The other day I went to shut off my headlights and the switch was hot.  Not red-hot, but hot.  Just out of curiosity I felt the trunk-pop button and it was hot too.  Any clues?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||08-22-2001||12:52 AM||||That normally means something has a bad ground and is grounding back thru another circuit. What, I wouldn't guess.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||12:52 AM||||Well the trunk switch could be hot because of the backlight.  I suppose warm would be ok for headlight switch...but maybe the headlight relay is going and drawing lost of juice through the switch.  Never heard of this one!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||08-22-2001||01:53 AM||||I had a headlight switch get hot when I was using the dimmer to dull the dash lights, the dimmer is a rheostat and if not on full or off they build up heat when the lights are dimmed as they increase resistance (which causes heat)to dim the lights. Not sure on the trunk light, maybe just warm normally.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-22-2001||01:56 AM||||There are 2 types of bulbs for the dash/switches. Could it be someone put in the "brighter" bulbs? (Brighter = more heat)||||reg||5
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-22-2001||07:54 AM||||trunk release was just from the backlite. I have some radio shack lighted rocker switches and after a few minutes there too hot to touch. Yes the headlite switch gets hot from the dash reostat. Its normal on all cars.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jaygee79||08-22-2001||10:14 AM||||I had the dimmer up as far as it will go without the dome lights being on.  And my trunk pop button doesn't light up.  It's supposed to, but doesn't.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-22-2001||02:17 PM||||id check to see if theres a short or intermittent short in the wiring to the trunk release. if the lite not working and switch is hot, thats not normal. The headlite switch will always be warm, no matter where the dimmers set when the lights are on. Ive even drilled a series of holes in the dash panel to the left of speedo beside the switch (u cant see them) to help keep the heat down and dash from getting warped.||||reg||1
Z||000008||recluse||08-22-2001||04:30 PM||||I don't know about the head light switch but on my old 86 GT the armrest right above the cigarette lighter used to get very hot (burn your arm if you were not carful hot) I still dont know what it was.  I used a radar detector and when it was unpluged it wouldn't do it.  But it does'nt do it on my 87 with a radar detector.||||reg||1
